# AINumbers self-operated trust policy for the F1 errata/revocation registry
# log, per C2SP tlog-policy.md grammar. Landed by REGISTRY-ERRATA-TILES-BUILD-1
# (REGISTRY-TILES-BUILD-SPEC.md §3.3, §6). Unlike rekor-pinned.tlog-policy and
# sigsum-generic-2025-1.tlog-policy above (both pin a THIRD-PARTY log's key),
# this file pins OUR OWN log's key: AINumbers is the operator of
# registry/errata, generated and served as static C2SP tlog-tiles files by
# scripts/gen-registry-errata.mjs.
#
# Checkpoint origin (first line of the signed note body, no trailing slash):
#   ainumbers.co/registry/errata
#
# Algorithm: Ed25519 (signed-note.md algorithm tag 0x01). Public key below is
# the raw 32-byte verify key, hex-encoded, generated 2026-08-18 via WebCrypto
# (mirrors register-sigsum.mjs's own `keygen` command). The matching PRIVATE
# key is held OUTSIDE this repo, at workspace-root
# research/registry-errata-log-key.priv.jwk.json (never committed — same
# internal-artifact fence as research/sigsum-key.priv.jwk.json and
# research/registry-lineage-log-key.priv.jwk.json), per the workspace
# CLAUDE.md path-ambiguity trap section.
#
# ⭐ NO WITNESS COSIGNING is defined for this log directly (single-operator
# log, per tlog-policy.md's "a policy without witness cosigning can be
# defined using a quorum none line", same deviation rekor-pinned.tlog-policy
# and ainumbers-registry-lineage.tlog-policy above document). Equivocation
# resistance instead comes from a SEPARATE, ADDITIVE mechanism (REGISTRY-
# TILES-BUILD-SPEC.md §2.1): every checkpoint this log publishes is ALSO
# submitted as a leaf to the public Sigsum log
# (chaingraph/policies/sigsum-generic-2025-1.tlog-policy governs verification
# of THAT anchor). The self-contained Sigsum anchor record is stored beside
# each checkpoint at registry/errata/checkpoint.sigsum-record.json. A
# consumer who checks the Sigsum record can detect (never "prevent" — the
# honest word per BUILD-SPEC §9) equivocation of this log's own head; a
# consumer who never checks is not protected, exactly as BUILD-SPEC §2.1
# states plainly.
#
# ⛔⛔ STALENESS (BUILD-SPEC §2.2, verbatim, inherited from FV-AGENTSURFACE-
# SPEC-1 §2 — never re-derive, never paraphrase): "Past expires_at, treat it
# as unknown-refresh-needed — not as continuing to hold, and not as false
# either." This sentence is published as a checkpoint EXTENSION LINE on every
